{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-deepseek-harness/f53f80cc-1f77-5d02-a862-99d59ffabdce/scratchpad/bench/runs/h1-harness-loop-sonnet-t4/cell-9qwBsu/src/limiter.js","content":"/**
 * Token-bucket rate limiter with one bucket per key.
 *
 * A bucket holds at most `capacity` tokens and gains `refillTokens` every
 * `refillIntervalMs`, spread evenly over that interval rather than granted in
 * lumps, so time that does not add up to a whole interval is still credited.
 * Buckets are created full, which is what allows an initial burst, and time
 * comes from an injectable clock so callers can drive it exactly.
 *
 * Internally a bucket's token count is tracked scaled by `refillIntervalMs`
 * (i.e. in units of tokens * milliseconds) so that refilling can be computed
 * with exact integer arithmetic: repeated small advances then credit exactly
 * what one large advance of the same total would.
